<title>UK: U.S., Japan keen to monitor EMU plans - Brittan.</title>
<headline>U.S., Japan keen to monitor EMU plans - Brittan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commission Vice-President Sir Leon Brittan said on Wednesday the United States and Japan had shown an increased interest in the planned European Monetary Union (EMU) because of the impact it could have on them.</p>
<p>Brittan was speaking in a BBC radio interview ahead of the annual European Union-Japan summit in the Netherlands later on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Asked whether EMU would be discussed at the summit, he said: &quot;I think they are very interested in EMU because they think it might affect them.</p>
<p>&quot;It's very noticeable that both the Americans and the Japanese have got much more interested in EMU in the last few months than they ever were because they see it coming and obviously it's going to have an impact.&quot;</p>
</text>
